hicago are finer than the Lincoln Park Zoo. It's world-class, yet admission is free; its winding, expansive grounds have the charm of age, yet its facilities are modern and the animals are healthy, happy, and personable.…"],["Elks National Veterans Memorial","sight",41.93232,-87.63994,"2750 N Lakeview Ave","Mon-Fri 9AM-5PM; also Sat Sun 10AM-5PM from 15 Apr-15 Nov","","","","r","This neoclassical veterans memorial is truly grand. Its interior is an extravagant ensemble of marble, bronze sculptures, stained glass, and huge murals."],["Lincoln Park Conservatory","sight",41.924,-87.6353,"2400 N Stockton Dr","9AM-5PM","","","","r","Built 1890-1895, the conservatory is right next to the zoo. Even though they're overshadowed by the animals next door, the plants receive an equal amount of care, and there are usually some eye-popping floral displays in the spring.…"],["Peggy Notebaert Nature Museum","sight",41.92681,-87.63532,"2430 N Cannon Dr","Mon-Fri 9AM-4:30PM, Sat Sun 10AM-5PM","","","","r","Carefully positioned within walking distance of the Lincoln Park Zoo in hopes of being parents' second stop while they're in the area, the Notebaert Nature Museum is... okay. Exhibits are geared toward kids and are sometimes hands-on.…"],["National Shrine of Saint Frances Xavier Cabrini","sight",41.92881,-87.63956,"2520 N Lakeview Ave","Tue-Fri 10AM-3PM, Sat 9AM-5PM, Sun 9AM-3PM","","","","r","Historically, spiritually and architecturally, the Shrine is a \"must see\" destination for Chicago visitors. The Shrine Honors the first American Citizen Saint and Patron of Immigrants in the Catholic Church. Designed by world renowned…"],["Tandoor Char House","restaurant",41.92072,-87.6374,"2119 N Clark St","Mon-Tue 11AM-10PM, Fri Sat 11AM-11PM, Sun 11AM-9PM","","","","r","Indian/Pakistani cuisine, good bite before the B.L.U.E.S. or the Kingston Mines."]]}